- [x] look into E2E encryption — investigated (Aug 2026). Real E2E needs per-message
      keys encrypted to both parties' public keys, since letters must be readable by
      two people who don't share a secret. A simpler "password is the key" scheme
      only works for single-user vaults (like Ente), not two-party mail. Given
      Penny Post's threat model (personal letters, mostly-trusted users) doesn't
      clearly call for it, and it would meaningfully complicate circulars, drafts,
      and the account-deletion flow — decided not to pursue for now. It would be good to add this to the About page though.
